#
# Failing control for math:TensorAxisIndexUniquenessConstraint: a rank-2 shape declares
# two distinct axis nodes that both claim index 0. Two axes agree with the rank and
# index 0 is zero or greater and below 2, so the count, bound and range laws hold; the
# repeated position is the only defect. Bound by ex:ecTensorAxisIndexDuplicate.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/tensor-shape-controls/> .

ex:shape a math:TensorShape ; math:tensorRank 2 ;
    math:shapeAxis ex:left, ex:right .
ex:left a math:TensorAxis ; math:axisIndex 0 .
ex:right a math:TensorAxis ; math:axisIndex 0 .
